  "decisions": [
    "The reference document's algorithms, IDL definitions and rendering rules describe user-agent behaviour, not source vocabulary, and are therefore not converted into registries.",
    "Content attribute event handlers (on*) are registered so that the compiler can reject them with a precise diagnostic instead of reporting an unknown attribute.",
    "The style content attribute is required by the standard but forbidden by RoboHTMLCompiler: it is registered and then rejected by the inline-CSS rule.",
    "Obsolete features are registered as deprecated so strict mode can reject them explicitly rather than silently ignoring them."
  ],
